It is indeed very Contra-like:
1. It made me rage;
2. My arm hurts after a play session from pressing buttons;
It should come as no surprise that it is best played with a controller.

Broken Sword 3
Pros:
- I enjoy the Broken Sword stories and characters;
- Certain of the puzzles are satisfying to complete;
Cons
- The controls are atrocious;
- The conversion to 3D was not kind. Too much of the game is spent moving the characters around awkwardly, while the samera switches and f***s up your direction continuously;
- There are far too many doors that are locked;
- Too many box puzzles;
- Even though I enjoyed the story, it wasn't as satisfying as (and kind of a departure from) the original broken sword. Without giving spoilers, it is too overtly supernatural;
Score - 5/10
Play it for the story or watch a let's play.

Neat little RPG-Maker-Style game. It's a mix of horror, comedy and some rather cute elements. Some of the riddles are actually not that easy, though I got almost everything right in my first try (
). Achievements are easy to earn, so you can add one more game to your "mom, get the camera" collection.
The game is about an hour long, so you won't miss anything big, while you're having fun with this cute little horror thingy.

Even though Broken Sword 3 departed from the point-and-click 2D adventure, I am trying to be open-minded and not afraid of changes, when it comes to games that I literally grew up with.
But in general:
+ Good story, nice dialogues;
+ The characters remain faithful to the first two games;
+ More cut-scenes than the previous 2 games;
+ You get to play with George and Nico equal time;
+ The character animations feel quite much human.
- They could've made the ending a bit more satisfying;
- TOO MUCH ♥♥♥♥ING MILLION-KILOMETERS-OF-CRATE-PUSHING "PUZZLES"!
- No, seriously. DO NOT PUT CRATE PUSHING PUZZLES IN YOUR GAME! EVER! If I wanted to play a game that you push crates, that game should not be named "Broken Sword".
Anyway, this game is pretty much enjoyable and I recommend it. But only after you finished the first 2 Broken Sword games.

Pro's:
